<article id="post-113" class="post-113 page type-page status-publish hentry">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">Welcome to the Town of Sunderland</h1>
	</header><!-- .entry-header -->

	<div class="entry-content">
		<p style="text-align: justify;">The Town of Sunderland is located within Bennington County, in Vermont´s southwest corner.  In recent years residents and visitors have branded this beautiful region nestled between the Taconic and Green Mountains as <a href="https://exploretheshires.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Shires of Vermont</a>.  Located between <a href="http://www.bennington.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bennington</a>, the South Shire, and <a href="https://www.manchestervermont.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Manchester</a>, the North Shire, Sunderland is surrounded by mountains and enriched by the waters of the famous Batten Kill that runs through the valley.  Sunderland and the towns around it have historically been a popular four season destination for those seeking an authentic Vermont experience.  You’ll find canoeing, tubing, camping, mountain biking, hiking and skiing close by.  All within a 4 hour drive from New York City, Hartford, Boston, Northern New Jersey and Canada.</p>
<h3 style="text-align: justify;"><strong>Latest News and Announcements:</strong></h3>
<p><strong>Election Day: Tuesday, November 3, 2026</strong></p>
<p>Polls are open from <strong>10:00 am to 7:00</strong> pm at the Sunderland Town Hall, 104 Mountainview Road.</p>
<p>Two votes will take place:</p>
<ul>
<li>General Election Ballot</li>
<li>Special Vote Ballot for the Sunderland Elementary School Property sale</li>
</ul>
<p>Please note: there are two separate ballots.</p>
<hr />
<p><strong>Town of Sunderland Completes Municipal Energy Resilience Projects</strong></p>
<p>The Town of Sunderland has completed energy efficiency improvements at the Town Hall and the Town Garage. The projects were supported by a $206,632.40 grant from Vermont’s Municipal Energy Resilience Program (MERP) and the Town’s Special Projects Fund, established by a voter-approved article in 2024.</p>
<p>At the Town Hall, improvements included the installation of a mini-split heating and cooling unit in the meeting room, interior LED lighting upgrades, and weather stripping on doors to reduce drafts and improve energy efficiency.</p>
<p>At the Town Garage, improvements included full replacement of wall and ceiling insulation, an electrical panel upgrade, installation of a ducted heat pump to replace the existing propane heating system as the building’s primary heat source, and LED lighting upgrades. The Town’s Special Projects Fund covered the cost of replacing the Town Garage roof.</p>
<p>Centerline Architects of Bennington served as project manager, while Pro-Builders Construction of Hoosick, New York, completed the Town Garage renovations. The Sunderland Energy Committee and the Bennington County Regional Commission also provided valuable support throughout the project.</p>
<p>These improvements represent an investment in Sunderland’s municipal infrastructure and reflect the Town’s commitment to responsible stewardship of taxpayer resources. The projects are intended to improve energy efficiency, enhance building comfort, and help manage long-term operating costs.</p>
<p>The Town of Sunderland thanks the Vermont Department of Buildings and General Services, Centerline Architects, Pro-Builders Construction, the Sunderland Highway Department, the Sunderland Energy Committee, the Bennington County Regional Commission, and the subcontractors and local businesses whose work helped make these improvements possible.</p>

